<title>LEBANON: Chirac questions Israeli oil drilling on Golan.</title>
<headline>Chirac questions Israeli oil drilling on Golan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac expressed apparent disapproval of an Israeli decision reported on Friday to approve oil drilling in the occupied Golan Heights.</p>
<p>Israel's Haaretz newspaper said Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu approved the drilling request by the state-owned National Oil Company. Netanyahu spokesman Shai Bazak said he was checking the report.</p>
<p>Asked about the report at a news conference in Beirut, on the fifth leg of his Middle East tour, Chirac said:</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think it was particularly well chosen to take this initiative but perhaps Mr Netanyahu has reasons to think otherwise.&quot;</p>
<p>Israel captured the Golan Heights from Syria in the 1967 Middle East war.</p>
</text>
